    "number": "Theorem 10",
    "quote": "Let $\\Deltamin \\in (0, 1/4)$, $K \\geq 4$, and $T \\geq \\max \\left\\{ \\frac{\\ln (K)}{16 \\Deltamin^2}, \\frac{\\ln (K)}{10 \\epsilon \\Deltamin} \\right\\}$. Then, for any $\\epsilon$-differentially private online learning algorithm for the full information setting, there is a distribution over reward vectors (with minimum gap $\\Deltamin$ as above) such that the optimal action is unique and the regret of the algorithm is lower bounded as $\\Omega \\left( \\max \\left\\{ \\frac{\\log (K)}{\\Deltamin}, \\frac{\\log (K)}{\\epsilon} \\right\\} \\right)$."
